# Distribution archives built for download.
#
# These are generated from the tracked source in trading/, so committing one
# would store a second, binary copy that goes stale the moment the code
# changes. Rebuild instead:
#
#   zip -rq ATLAS-trading-system.zip trading/ \
#     -x "trading/frontend/node_modules/*" -x "trading/backend/.venv/*" \
#     -x "*/__pycache__/*" -x "trading/.env" -x "trading/data/atlas.db*"
#
ATLAS-trading-system.zip
*.zip

# Secrets, anywhere in the tree. The project-level trading/.gitignore already
# covers this; repeated here so a stray .env outside that folder is caught too.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
